It looks like the "travel" algorithm is checking
connectivity, but not including your burden in the
check, just checking burden restrictions move by
move, so that when you get to the cell shown, you
can't squeeze through to the cell northwest of it,
so travel moves you right instead, temporarily
disqualifying that northwestward path. Now, though,
when travel recomputes your path, the path left and
then northwest still looks shortest, burden no
longer being considered, so you get moved left, but
cannot squeeze through to the northwest on the next
move.

Lather, rinse, repeat.

